{
  "comment": "Slice D T2 hook-frame corpus. `harnesses` is the closed id set and the response key each one expects — a null key means the harness takes the plain context body (OpenCode's in-process mapper; Codex until the T7 gate confirms its shape). `frames` are well-formed native session-event payloads, one per harness shape, with WORKSPACE substituted for the test's Git workspace. `malformed` frames are byte sequences the read path must refuse with a bounded code, rendering no payload.",
